ld/merge authorization before implementation depending on the ADR can proceed. In this overnight non-interactive run I can still do research/planning later, but I cannot autonomously satisfy the HOLD/MERGE approval requirement. Moving to other actionable non-ADR tickets meanwhile.","timestamp":1788425576169232001},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation note: ADR 0115 was taken on origin/main before Gerrit submit, causing an add/add conflict on docs/adr/.numbers/0115. I rebased and regenerated the ADR index/markers, so this ticket's decision record is now docs/adr/0116-retire-config-aliases.md. The declared file_impact still covers the change (docs/adr, docs/adr/.numbers, docs/api-stability.md).","timestamp":1788547013156144081}],"created_at":1788421598951045001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c6d4552e-05a7-4ba5-9327-b082a88f6ce5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1b07-c4c8-c523-43b4"},{"link_uuid":"9efe159b-04d8-4e5d-a700-e9a122ec6868","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"42b3-e650-005e-476b"},{"link_uuid":"f9f2eb2c-3c03-4e9f-8d22-b4d7a3889e26","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ce97-dd31-6cd0-409d"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe Janitor approval for parent story 038d authorizes removing eight long-lived env/config aliases instead of keeping them as permanent ergonomic renames. That approval explicitly chose **clean removal for simplification (no expected clients)**: follow-on work must remove the alias declarations and active parsing/warning paths, not convert these aliases to fail-loud tombstones. Before code or published docs change, the project needs an ADR that records the approval, names each canonical replacement, defines the removal order for the dependent chain, and distinguishes this pre-1.0 operator-approved cleanup from the stronger public/wire/persisted-data compatibility contracts.\n\n## Approach\n\nAllocate the next ADR number through `docs/adr/.numbers`, write the ADR in the standard house style, and record the governing policy for this chain:\n\n| Removed alias | Canonical replacement |\n| --- | --- |\n| `REBAR_NO_SYNC` | `REBAR_SYNC_PULL=off` |\n| `COMPACT_THRESHOLD` | `REBAR_COMPACT_THRESHOLD` |\n| `SCRATCH_BASE_DIR` | `REBAR_SCRATCH_BASE_DIR` |\n| `REBAR_ACLI_TIMEOUT` | `REBAR_JIRA_CLI_TIMEOUT` |\n| `RECONCILER_ABSENT_GET_BUDGET` | `REBAR_RECONCILER_DELETION_PROBE_LIMIT` |\n| `REBAR_ID_GUARD_MODE=warn` | `REBAR_UNSAFE_ID_GUARD_BYPASS=true` |\n| `REBAR_VERIFY_OVERLAP_ENABLED` | `REBAR_VERIFY_SUGGEST_DUPLICATE_TICKETS` |\n| `verify.overlap_enabled` | `verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets` |\n\nThe ADR must cite the current authoritative code locations (`src/rebar/_deprecations.py`, `src/rebar/_config_sources.py`, and `src/rebar/_config_sections.py`) for the live aliases and cite the 038d operator approval for the clean-removal rationale. It should call out `REBAR_NO_SYNC` and `REBAR_ID_GUARD_MODE` as transformed-semantics aliases (inverse pull and id-guard bypass) that need explicit migration text, while still applying the same clean-removal policy to the remaining inert renames. It must define the dependency order: this ADR first, then 7370 removes/tombstones only as directed by the implementation plan, then 038d removes live aliases, then 1a63 publishes docs/release notes.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `docs/adr/.numbers`\n- new ADR under `docs/adr/`\n- `docs/api-stability.md` for the minimal cross-reference from config stability policy\n\n## Testing\n\nRun `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py`, `python scripts/check_docs_index.py`, and `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`. Also verify with grep that `docs/api-stability.md` references ADR 0116 and still separately documents the strong public/wire/persisted-data contracts (`--output json` schemas, MCP schemas, event schema, public Python facade, and persisted-data migrations/readers) so this config-alias cleanup is not over-applied.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The ADR is Accepted, uses the generator-assigned ADR number, and cites the 038d operator approval as clean removal for simplification with no expected clients.\n- [x] The ADR records all eight removed aliases and their canonical replacements exactly as listed in the plan table.\n- [x] The ADR explains that follow-on implementation removes alias declarations and active parsing/warning paths rather than preserving these aliases as permanent aliases or converting them into fail-loud tombstones.\n- [x] The ADR calls out `REBAR_NO_SYNC` and `REBAR_ID_GUARD_MODE` as transformed-semantics aliases requiring explicit migration text.\n- [x] The ADR distinguishes this pre-1.0 config/env alias cleanup from public/wire/persisted-data compatibility contracts.\n- [x] `docs/api-stability.md` contains a minimal cross-reference to ADR 0116 and still documents the separate strong contracts for JSON/MCP schemas, the event schema, the public Python facade, and persisted-data compatibility.\n- [x] `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py`, `python scripts/check_docs_index.py`, and `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/adr/.numbers","reason":"allocate the next ADR number"},{"path":"docs/adr","reason":"record the approved alias-removal policy"},{"path":"docs/api-stability.md","reason":"cross-reference the new policy if needed"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["parent","038d-f5ff-b371-4ba5"],["relates_to","1b07-c4c8-c523-43b4"],["relates_to","42b3-e650-005e-476b"],["relates_to","ce97-dd31-6cd0-409d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"038d-f5ff-b371-4ba5","parent_status_uuid":"b940d11f-23a0-489d-8a1c-50fd70cd4adb","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor","config","breaking-change","compatibility"],"ticket_id":"8ca7-28c5-c5c4-4f32","ticket_type":"task","title":"ADR: retire config aliases","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["43730100-c6a6-405d-87a6-4e8c895edb63","4d0c742b-1210-4f9b-8a41-32e827521589","12f49dec-f823-41cd-b5a3-0fede13ad1d9","b940d11f-23a0-489d-8a1c-50fd70cd4adb","ebb23db4-148a-4b3b-96bb-34c0ca249aaf","c6d4552e-05a7-4ba5-9327-b082a88f6ce5","9efe159b-04d8-4e5d-a700-e9a122ec6868","f9f2eb2c-3c03-4e9f-8d22-b4d7a3889e26","0a9cf66a-ea13-412b-873b-84b83a7278f3","c24d6b4f-4bbc-4627-89e3-c06eb67491f8","d2cedc7f-8afc-4a48-86eb-e2567526346d"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788547715788611327,"uuid":"6db19fe4-decc-47b9-8978-c47050a31f7b"}